    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0564" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/12094</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-04T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 6, 4.17
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5579. Baron [de] Vaux, Counselor Austrian Legation, called
                    on Francis McNutt, American citizen, and impressed on him
                    immediate danger of Bolshevik menace in Austria and her insistence that American
                    troops be sent to occupy Vienna to prevent disorders, at the same time that a
                    statement be made explaining that they came in friendly spirit to safeguard the
                    peace.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
